  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Hulk has a set of distinct points PPP in the 2D plane. His signature move is HulkHulkHulk SmashSmashSmash. He performed HulkHulkHulk SmashSmashSmash on the set PPP which caused the points to change, and so he obtained a new set of points P′P'P′.\n\nMore formally, HulkHulkHulk SmashSmashSmash makes the new set P′P'P′ in the following way:\n\n\nInitially, let P′P'P′ be empty.\nFor every PiP_iPi​ and PjP_jPj​ such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N , add the mid point of PiP_iPi​ and PjP_jPj​ to the set P′P'P′ (only if it didn't exist in it already).\nSo, P′P'P′ is the set of midpoints of line segments connecting pairs of distinct points of PPP.\nNote that points from PPP do not necessarily have to be in P′P'P′. See the samples below for a graphical example.\n\nFind the number of points of P′P'P′ which lie on the convex hull of P′P'P′. A point is said to lie on the convex hull if the shape of the convex hull is changed when this point is removed.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the size of PPP.\nThe next NNN lines contain two space-separated integers each, where the iii-th line contains Pi.x,Pi.yP_i.x,P_i.yPi​.x,Pi​.y denoting the x-coordinate and y-coordinate of the iii-th point.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer - the number of points of P′P'P′ which lie on its convex hull.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\leq T \\leq 201≤T≤20",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−5⋅108≤Pi.x,Pi.y≤5⋅108-5 \\cdot 10^8 \\leq P_i.x, P_i.y \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^8−5⋅108≤Pi​.x,Pi​.y≤5⋅108",
      "The convex hull of the input set PPP has positive area",
      "Sum of NNN over all tests cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (20 points):**",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10310^3103",
      "**Subtask 2 (80 points):**",
      "Original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
