        "input": "2\n7\n1 7\n-6 -5\n1 -6\n-6 7\n-4 3\n-2 6\n-3 -6\n4\n1 8\n1 4\n1 0\n5 4",
        "output": "8\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the below images, the set of points PPP is denoted by the color pink, the set of points P′P'P′ is denoted by the color green. The blue point is the origin.\n\n\nThe below image represents the first test case\n\n\n\n\n\nThe below image represents the second test case\n\n\n\n\n\nNote that by our definition, points (1,4)(1, 4)(1,4) and (3,4)(3, 4)(3,4) are not considered to lie on the convex hull of P′P'P′, because removing one of them does not change the shape of the hull."
      }
